<title>RUSSIA: Petersburg Russia port 96 oil product exports dive.</title>
<headline>Petersburg Russia port 96 oil product exports dive.</headline>
<dateline>ST PETERSBURG, Russia 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product exports through Russia's northeastern port St Petersburg fell sharply to 2.98 million tonnes in 1996 from 4.04 million in 1995, Yevgeny Tabarovsky, head of the port's licensing section said Friday.</p>
<p>He said four loading firms specialising in oil products for export had operated at the port last year, out of a total of 20 companies dealing with loading all types of goods.</p>
<p>The licensing division gave the following information for those four companies --</p>
<p>OIL PRODUCTS EXPORTED THROUGH ST PETERSBURG IN 1996</p>
<p>			  (BY COMPANY, IN MILLION TONNES)</p>
<p>				   1996	    1995 OAO Morskoi Port</p>
<p> St Petersburg		 1.37	    2.22 ZAO Peterburgsky</p>
<p> Neftyanoi Terminal	  0.84	    1.13 AOZT Perstiko</p>
<p>0.71 0.67 AOZT Intekhport 0.07 0.02</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
